# Tutorial documentation

When adding or changing a user-visible feature or flow:

- Update `resources/js/pages/Tutorial.vue` in the same implementation.
- Explain the user task, the control or navigation used, and any important limits or side effects.
- Add or update a tutorial TOC entry when the change deserves its own section.
- Keep the tutorial accurate after UI, behavior, terminology, and workflow changes—not only after net-new features.
- Refresh `public/images/guide/` screenshots (desktop and mobile) whenever the UI they show changes—labels, controls, layout, or stage chrome.
- Update the public FAQ/backlog entry too when the feature is represented on `resources/js/pages/BetaTesterFaqs.vue`.

Before finishing feature work, verify that the tutorial describes what now works, that guide images match the live UI, and that it does not promise deferred behavior.
